<h2 class="doc_title">Dr. Vinod Kumar Bassi vs The State Of U.P And Anr. on 10 July, 2014</h2>
<h2 class="doc_title">Dr. Vinod Kumar Bassi vs The State Of U.P And Anr. on 10 July, 2014</h2>

<h3 class="doc_author">Author: <a href="/search/?formInput=authorid:a-lamba">Ajai Lamba</a></h3>

<h3 class="doc_bench">Bench: <a href="/search/?formInput=benchid:a-lamba">Ajai Lamba</a></h3>

<pre id="pre_1">




HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE AT ALLAHABAD, LUCKNOW BENCH
 
 

?Court No. - 26
 

 
Case :- U/S 482/378/407 No. - 2998 of 2014
 

 
Applicant :- Dr. Vinod Kumar Bassi
 
Opposite Party :- The State Of U.P And Anr.
 
Counsel for Applicant :- Amrendra Singh
 
Counsel for Opposite Party :- Govt. Advocate
 

 
Hon&#x27;ble Ajai Lamba,J.
 
</pre><p data-structure="PetArg" id="p_1">1. In the short contention of the learned counsel appearing for the petitioner, the proceedings have been initiated without conducting enquiry under Sub-Section 1 of <a href="/doc/1149595/" id="a_1">Section 202</a> of the Code of Criminal Procedure having been made.  
</p> 
<p data-structure="RespArg" id="p_2">2. Admittedly, the petitioner is living in Lucknow, whereas complaint has been lodged in Hardoi.
</p> 
<p data-structure="CDiscource" id="p_3">3. Issue notice to respondent no.2 through Chief Judicial Magistrate, Hardoi, returnable on 18.8.2014.
</p> 
<p data-structure="Conclusion" id="p_4">4. List on 18.8.2014. 
</p> 
<p data-structure="Conclusion" id="p_5">5. In the meantime, further proceedings shall remain stayed till the next date of listing.
</p> 
<p data-structure="Conclusion" id="p_6">Order Date :- 10.7.2014
 
A.Nigam
 



 




 

 
 
    
      
  
 </p>
